ollowing:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x=2\\lambda x \\\\ -2y=2\\lambda y\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}x(2-\\lambda )=0 \\\\ y(\\lambda +1)=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we break it up into several cases:\n\n- Assuming $x=0$ in the first equation of the system, the constraint condition ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4=0$ implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-4 & =0\\,⇒\\,y=\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical points $(0,-2),(0,2).$\n\n- Assuming $\\lambda =2$ in the first equation of the system, the second equation of the system implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2+1)=0\\,⇒\\,y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the constraint condition ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4=0$ implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical points $(2,0),(-2,0).$\n\nTherefore, $f$ has possible extreme values at the points\n\n$$\n(0,\\pm 2),\\,(\\pm 2,0).\n$$\n\nWe evaluate $f$ at these points. These are given in the following table:\n\n| $(x,y)$ | $(0,\\pm 2)$ | $(\\pm 2,0)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x,y)$ | $-3$ | $9$ |\n\nTherefore, the function reaches a minimum value at the points $(0,\\pm 2)$ and its minimum value is $-3.$" 13194139536009 true] [17592186379258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379259 13194139536009 true] [17592186379258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379260 13194139536009 true] [17592186379258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379261 13194139536009 true] [17592186379258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379262 13194139536009 true] [17592186379258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379263 13194139536009 true] [17592186379258 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536009 true] [17592186379258 1041 "selection" 13194139536009 true] [17592186379258 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379260 13194139536009 true] [17592186379258 1110 #uuid "6173ad26-93ee-533b-9fca-b7a634522cf2" 13194139536009 true] [17592186379259 1034 "-9" 13194139536009 true] [17592186379259 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536009 true] [17592186379259 1111 #uuid "bcc5194d-0338-5f62-b5b1-afc0a859588e" 