\\\ 2z=2\\lambda z\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}(4-{\\lambda }^{2})x=0 \\\\ (4-{\\lambda }^{2})y=0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we break it up into several cases:\n\n- First, assume that $\\lambda \\ne 1$ and $\\lambda \\ne \\pm 2.$ Then, the solution of the above system is $x=y=z=0.$ But this contradicts the constraint $g(x,y,z)=0.$\n\n- Next, assume that $\\lambda =-2.$ Then we must have $x=y$ and $z=0.$ But this also contradicts the constraint $g(x,y,z)=0.$\n\n- Now, assume that $\\lambda =1.$ Then, by the first and second equations, we must have $x=y=0.$ Also, by the constraint $g(x,y,z)=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}-4=0\\,⇒\\,z=\\pm 2.\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical points $(0,0,\\pm 2).$\n\n- Finally, assume that $\\lambda =2.$ Then we must have $x=-y$ and $z=0.$ Also, by the constraint $g(x,y,z)=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n-(-y)y-4=0\\,⇒\\,y=\\pm 2.\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical points $(∓2,\\pm 2,0).$\n\nWe evaluate $f$ at each of these points. These are given in the following table:\n\n| $\\,(x,y,z)\\,$ | $\\,(0,0,\\pm 2)\\,$ | $\\,(∓2,\\pm 2,0)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,f(x,y,z)\\,$ | $\\,7\\,$ | $\\,11\\,$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function reaches a minimum value at the points $(0,0,\\pm 2),$ and its minimum value is $7.$" 13194139536009 true] [17592186379265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379266 13194139536009 true] [17592186379265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379267 13194139536009 true] [17592186379265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379268 13194139536009 true] [17592186379265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379269 13194139536009 true] [17592186379265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379270 13194139536009 true] [17592186379265 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536009 true] [17592186379265 1041 "selection" 13194139536009 true] [17592186379265 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379268 13194139536009 true] [17592186379265 1110 #uuid "aeba2af3-e438-55ff-b552-30b57c0ac261" 13194139536009 true] [17592186379266 1034 "9" 13194139536009 true] [17592186379266 1103 #edb/re